## Why This Is Asked

Tests beginners learn to control external dependencies (maps, geolocation) and test isolation. This prompts demonstration of end-to-end coverage for critical user journeys while addressing flakiness through retries and data cleanup.

## Key Concepts

- Test data isolation per run
- Geolocation and permission prompts
- Network throttling and flakiness handling
- Stubbing external APIs (maps)
- Session cleanup to prevent leakage

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright example: mock geolocation and slow network
const context = await browser.newContext({
  geolocation: { latitude: 37.7749, longitude: -122.4194 }
});
const page = await context.newPage();
await context.overridePermissions('https://ride.example.com', ['geolocation']);
await page.route('**/maps/api/**', route => route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ predictions: [] }) }));
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this test to run in CI with parallel isolation?
- How would you diagnose a flaky GPS prompt in CI?

